# Project Rules

- Read README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md before changing the project.
- Use React, TypeScript, and vinext App Router conventions; builds use Vite/Nitro.
- Use pnpm with the committed lockfile and Node.js 22.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested behavior and reuse existing module boundaries.
- Keep files at most 500 lines, functions under 50 lines, and lines under 100 characters.
- Prefer server components unless browser state or interaction requires a client component.
- Validate provider responses and preserve unknown, zero, stale, and failed states distinctly.
- Never retry management commands automatically or report acceptance as completion.
- Use synthetic provider fixtures in tests; never operate a real VPS during verification.
- Do not commit credentials, local environment files, real logs, or private VPS screenshots.
- Run relevant checks before committing; CI also verifies the compiled Vercel output.

